claim.claim-text:
a valve body comprising a body inlet (18) coaxial to a first axis (20) and a plurality of body outlets (22a, 22b, 22c) each oriented at an angle (33) transverse to the first axis;
a spherical flow control element (14) disposed within a cavity (94) of the valve body;
wherein the flow control element comprises a ball inlet (24) having a ball inlet area radially arranged about the first axis, and a ball outlet (28) having a ball outlet area larger than the ball inlet area, radially arranged at the transverse angle to the first axis, the flow control element rotatable about the first axis to selectively align the ball outlet with each of the plurality of body outlets separately and to overlap the ball outlet with portions of two of the body outlets; and
wherein the body outlets have a cross-sectional flow area tapering down from adjacent to the flow control element to an end connection.

a like plurality of outlet valve seat assembly recesses (68), each valve seat recess radially arranged about a respective one of the body outlets, each valve seat recess receiving a respective outlet valve seat assembly (44A) in sealing engagement between the valve body and the flow control element;
a like plurality of resilient members (46), each biased between the valve body and a respective one of the outlet valve seat assemblies; and
an inlet sleeve assembly (48A) radially arranged about the body inlet in sealing, biased engagement between the valve body and the flow control element.

the valve body comprises a lower main body (12) sealingly engaged with an upper bonnet (62);
the body inlet is disposed through the main body;
a portion of each body outlet is formed through the main body and a remaining portion of each body outlet is formed by the bonnet;
a lower portion (60) of each outlet seat recess is formed into the main body, whereby a corresponding lower portion of each resilient member is biased against the main body;
an upper portion (66) of each outlet seat recess is formed into the bonnet, whereby a corresponding upper portion of each resilient member is biased against the bonnet.

(a) providing a multiport valve of any preceding claim;
(b) rotating the flow control element to switch alignment of the ball outlet from one of the body outlets to another one of the body outlets;
(c) continuously flowing process media through the valve while rotating the flow control element; and
(d) overlapping the ball outlet with portions of two of the body outlets to avoid interrupting the flowing process media through the valve while rotating the flow control element.

(1) continuously supplying steam to a plurality of steam purge inlets to the cavity;
(2) rotating the flow control element to switch alignment of the ball outlet from one of the body outlets to another one of the body outlets while maintaining the steam supply; and
(3) draining steam and process media from the cavity after the alignment switching.
